2026-09-27T10:25:30.6759297Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6759685Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6760338Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6760660Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6760877Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6761320Z ================
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6761560Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6761784Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6762318Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6762575Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6762719Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6763021Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6763169Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6763383Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6763759Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6764105Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6764723Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6765166Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6765276Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6765742Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6766256Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6766492Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6766765Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6767130Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6767221Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6767446Z ========
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6767590Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6768538Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6769550Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6769793Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6770503Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6771152Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6771686Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6772238Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6772745Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6773058Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6773166Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6773879Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6774075Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6774896Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6775752Z 
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6776270Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6777024Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:25:30.6777213Z 
